<Base title="About the toolkit" active="about">
<div class="container reading-page"><a class="back-link" href={withBase()}>← Explore the toolkit</a><h1>Useful work.<br /><span class="muted">Inspectable source.</span></h1><div class="prose"><p class="lead">Agent Toolkit is Jordan Davis’s public collection of agent-assisted engineering skills, workflows, and selected developer tools.</p><h2>Small pieces that earn their place</h2><p>The goal is not to collect the most prompts. It is to make useful engineering procedures understandable: bound the task, establish ownership, use existing tools, and hand back evidence.</p><h2>Three kinds of contribution</h2><p><strong>Original</strong> means written for this repository. The first starter skills are newly created, AI-assisted drafts—not an inventory of private production workflows. <strong>Adapted</strong> work must identify its upstream source, revision, license, and changes. <strong>Curated</strong> entries link to other authors without claiming their work.</p><h2>Evidence, not badges</h2><p>The initial skills are experimental. Structural checks test the package shape; they do not establish that a host activates a skill correctly or that its outputs improve real tasks. Compatibility and usage claims require recorded evaluations.</p><h2>Credit where it belongs</h2><p>The catalog approach takes inspiration from <a href="https://ecc.tools/skills">ECC</a>. Focused skill packaging takes inspiration from <a href="https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-skills">Vercel Agent Skills</a> and the <a href="https://agentskills.io/specification">Agent Skills specification</a>. External projects retain their authorship and terms. No upstream skill bodies are copied into this initial collection.</p><h2>Public by intention</h2><p>No private knowledge-base exports, machine configurations, credentials, or product code belong here. Hiding an item from the website does not make a public repository file private.</p><h2>Help improve it</h2><p>Bring a real use case, a small example, and an honest account of what was tested. Read the <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>contribution guide</a> and <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/docs/ROADMAP.md`}>roadmap</a>. A license for original repository content has not yet been selected; do not assume the upstream projects’ licenses apply to this code.</p></div></div>
</Base>
